<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/732">732</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi was the Umayyad governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> in 721 and again from 730. In 732 he led a large raid across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a> and advanced towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>, but was defeated and killed by the Frankish leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours">Battle of Tours</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a>). The battle marked the limit of Muslim expansion into western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-al-ghafiqi.jpg" alt="Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi" width="184" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles de Steuben · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdul_Rahman_Al_Ghafiqi.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
